Documentation: only for the parts that are built.

The manual pages, help volumes and information library were made for
every part, whatever configure left out. With dtinfo, dtdocbook, dtksh or
dtappbuilder disabled, their documentation is now left out too:
- man/Makefile.am: the pages of dtbuilder, dtcodegen, dtbuilderaction and
  ttsnoop (dtappbuilder), dtksh and ksh-cde (dtksh), dtdocbook and
  dtdocbook2infolib (dtdocbook), and dtinfo with the DtInfo and DtMmdb
  interfaces (dtinfo) join their sections only when that part is built;
- help: AppBuilder.sdl and Infomgr.sdl, and their graphics, likewise;
- en_US.UTF-8/Makefile.am: guides, the information library, is made only
  with dtinfo; the manual pages still read their sources from it;
- without dtdocbook, the pages and help volumes are made with its
  configured dtdocbook2man and dtdocbook2sdl, which take the locations of
  instant and the DocBook files from the environment (dtdcbk_libdir,
  dtdcbk_libexecdir, dtdcbk_datarootdir); doc_utils' wrappers, which point
  them at the tree's own dtdocbook build, are used when it is built.
With every part enabled the same files are made as before.

